.B \&.sort(state: &'a SortState<K>)
The sort state to show (arrows on the headers, the cards' sort control). The table does not sort anything: sort the rows you pass in with \fBSortState::apply\fR.
.TP
.B \&.density(density: Density)
How roomy the rows are: \fBDensity::Default\fR, or \fBDensity::Compact\fR for a dense list. It sets the height of a row (virtualized tables) and the air above and below a cell.
.TP
.B \&.header(show: bool)
Whether the header row shows (default yes): the column titles, with the sort arrows of the sortable ones (see \fBsort\fR and \fBon_sort\fR). The header is part of the table; there is no separate header widget to keep in step.
.TP
.B \&.row_height(px: f32)
The height of a row in px, in place of the density's (\fBrow_height_of\fR). Only a virtualized table has a fixed row height.
.TP
.B \&.virtualized(total: usize, first: usize)
The rows passed to \fBnew\fR are a window of a long list: \fBtotal\fR rows, the first one passed being row \fBfirst\fR, each as tall as the density says (or \fBrow_height\fR) plus a 1 px hairline. Only those are built; spacers stand in for the rest. See \fBprimitives::virtualize\fR; give \fBViewport::window\fR \fBpitch\fR of the same height.
